    "summary": "High‑energy Dark Star → Eyes of the World → Half‑Step and stellar jams",
    "blurb": "Features an inspired Dark Star → Eyes of the World → Mississippi Half‑Step suite, plus a smoking China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider. Jerry delivers soaring solos on Greatest Story Ever Told and the extended jam, while the band maintains relentless momentum throughout both sets.",
    "review": "The February 26, 1973 show at Pershing Municipal Auditorium captures the Dead in top form during a high‑energy stretch of their early‑’73 run. The first set rolls through tight rockers and folk‑blues before launching into a blistering China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that sets the tone for an adventurous night. The second set shines with a monumental Dark Star → Eyes Of The World → Mississippi Half‑Step Uptown Toodeloo suite, where Jerry’s inspired leads soar over Phil’s solid yet occasionally cue‑missed bass work on Tennessee Jed. Greatest Story Ever Told provides another showcase for Garcia’s lyrical soloing, and the band rides the groove through Playing In The Band with unrelenting drive. While the soundboard source is generally clear, Billy’s ride cymbal sits forward in the mix, which can be a bit intrusive, but it also underscores the propulsive rhythm that powers this performance.",
